{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.62,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "extra_component",
      "components": ["J2", "U11", "U2"],
      "pins": ["J2.1", "J2.2", "U11.13", "U2.1", "U2.2"],
      "nets": ["/Microcontroller/NET0016", "GND"],
      "observed": "The netlist contains a 2-pin screw terminal J2 in the Microcontroller sheet. J2 pin 1 is connected to GND and J2 pin 2 is connected to /Microcontroller/NET0016, the same net as ESP32 GPIO1 and the TPS1H200AQDGNRQ1 IN/DIAG_EN inputs. No MAX31855 thermocouple input is connected to J2.",
      "expected": "The specification describes screw terminals only for the three thermocouple channels and the heater output. The GPIO1/heater-control net should drive the high-side switch input and the status LED, not an external screw terminal that can be shorted to ground.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"J2\") (value \"Screw_Terminal_01x02\") ... (property (name \"Sheetname\") (value \"Microcontroller\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"6\") (name \"/Microcontroller/NET0016\") ... (node (ref \"J2\") (pin \"2\") ... (node (ref \"U11\") (pin \"13\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"1\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"2\") ..."
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"8\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"J2\") (pin \"1\") ..."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "IN/DIAG_EN (pins 1/2) are both driven from ESP32 GPIO1 (net `/Microcontroller/HEATER`)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If a wire or short is attached across J2, GPIO1 and the TPS1H200 input are pulled to ground, preventing the heater from being enabled and potentially overloading the ESP32 output. Even when unused, this is an unintended user-accessible short path to the heater-control net.",
      "confidence": 0.62
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Most power, SPI, thermocouple, fan, and heater connectivity matches the specification, but the netlist includes an extra screw terminal J2 tied between the GPIO1 heater-control net and GND, which is not part of the intended design and can disable or fault the heater control if connected."
}

